-- title:
--   Ends, residue discs and nodal cover over a supersingular place
-- statement:
--   The ambient data are a prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`). Further: a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,M')$ over the residue field $\kappa_A=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ which (`hW`) consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. of the rational affine geometric places $w$ with $w(\,j\,)$ in the supersingular $j$-set `ssJSet q`; the inclusion `hle` of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$ into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base-changed function field of level $q^2M'$ with level group `levelH q M'`; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,M')$ (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` tracing $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, a degree-preserving map on places compatible with divisors), together with the coefficientwise compatibility `hR₀`: a Laurent series over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is its coefficientwise reduction; and a chosen $s\in W$.
--
--   The small-field data consist of an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0\cap A$ such that $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hdvr`, `hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$ (`hκ`). The auxiliary data comprise a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. The layer data are a family $K:\iota\to$ intermediate fields of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$, each finite over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_n\subseteq K_n$ tracing $A$ (`hAn`), an index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0}\le K_n$ for all $n$, and the cofinality `hKcof`: every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is contained in some $K_n$. In addition there is $\pi_t\in A$ with $\pi_t^{q^2-1}=q$, and the tameness hypothesis `htame`: every element $\tau$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ whose tame character at $\pi_t$ is trivial fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise. Finally, the base presentation consists of $K_b=\bot$ (the copy of $k_0$), a valuation subring $A_b\subseteq K_b$ tracing $A$, and a generator $\varpi_b\neq 0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   With $k_0$ acting on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ satisfying four clauses: $F_0$ consists exactly of those $f$ all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $k_0$; the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ adjoined to $F_0$ generate everything; $F_0$ is stable under the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every index $\zeta$ of primitive $q$-th roots of unity; and a linear disjointness clause: if $K'$ is finite over $k_0$, the $c_i\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ ($i<m$) are linearly independent over $K'$ and the $a_i$ lie in the compositum of $F_0$ with the image of $K'$, then $\sum_i c_ia_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$.
--
--   It is then asserted, for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$, every subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure, given that the class of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ lies in `R₀.integers` (`hjR`) with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$ (`hjs`), that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,q$ lies in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ (`hJK`), and that $a_0\in k_0\cap A$ satisfies the Hasse relation $\mathrm{res}_A(a_0)^q=s(\,\overline{j}\,)$ (`hpin`), and every finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$, the following implication.
--
--   The antecedent is a single long conjunction, whose groups are as follows (their content is summarised here, no clause being passed over). Valuative normalisation: $W_0$ traces $A$ on $k_0$, is a discrete valuation ring, and has maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$. Specialisation clause at $s$: for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose base change lies in `R₀.integers`, if $g$ has a pole at no place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ where $j$ has none, and if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue equals $s$ evaluated at that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $g$ and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. Equivariance: membership in $W_0$ is invariant under the level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. Chart block for $B$: the structure map $A_b\to B$ is the inclusion of constants; $B$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the image of $K_b$, and every element of that compositum is a fraction of elements of $B$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; $B/(\varpi_b)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $B\subseteq W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime; $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ away from $\varpi_b$, that is, $f\in W_0$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\varpi_b\nmid h$; the image of $\mathrm{jq}$ lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under the level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; there is an element $b$ of $B\cap F_0$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which traces $A$, contains $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal and makes $j$ integral in the strong sense that every monic polynomial over $k_0\cap A$ evaluated at $j$ is a unit of $V$; for each $s'\in W$ with $s'\neq s$ there is likewise an element of $B\cap F_0$ lying in no valuation subring of $F_0$ that traces $A$ and satisfies the specialisation clause centred at $s'$; and a Drinfeld-curve clause: for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on $\kappa_A$, every witness that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa_A$ is a domain and every index $\zeta$, there are a subgroup $C$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa_A\,C$ with $\#C=2\cdot\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, with kernel $(\varpi_b)$, restricting on constants to the residue map of $A$, with $\mathrm{quotField}$ the field of fractions of the image of $\rho$, with image characterised by lying in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa_A$ inside the Drinfeld function field, and equivariant for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction pair $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ lies in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, the level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ matching the Drinfeld $H$-action. Node block: `nodes` has $q+1$ elements; there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$, generated by the constants from $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set, contained in every node and with each node the localisation of $B_c$ at its own units; the level automorphisms permute the nodes, and for each index $\zeta$ the permutation action of $\Gamma_0(M')$ on the nodes is transitive; distinct nodes are separated by an element that is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; every valuation subring of $F_0$ tracing $A$ and satisfying the specialisation clause at $s$ either contains $B$ or dominates some node; and each node $O$ is contained in $W_0$, is local and noetherian, traces $A$, has every element congruent to a constant from $k_0\cap A$ modulo its non-units, and carries a crossing-model presentation: an exponent $E_0\ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{2\cdot\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\cdot v$ for a unit $v$ of $k_0\cap A$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$ and a unit $u$ of $O$ with $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$, and an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the completion of $A\cap k_0$ at parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, carrying constants to constants and $c_x,c_y$ to unit multiples of $U$ and $V$; $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ while $c_x$ is a unit there; the Hasse germ $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,q-a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ and is carried by $\iota$ to a unit multiple of $V^{e}$ with $e\ge 1$; there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, tracing $A$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, possessing an element $t$ for which a polynomial over $k_0\cap A$ with $t$ a root modulo the maximal ideal has all coefficients in the maximal ideal, with $c_x$ in its maximal ideal and $c_y$ a unit, and with the order of vanishing of the $g$ above detected by vanishing of the $R_0$-residue, the latter lying in the valuation subring of $s$ forcing the image of $g$ into $O$ and congruent there to the corresponding constant; and there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ contained in $B\cap O$, whose elements have poles only where $j$ does, such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at its units, every element of $F_0$ is a fraction of elements of $B_x$, $B_x$ is generated by the constants from $k_0\cap A$ and a finite set, and $B_x$ contains an element lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that traces $A$, contains $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, makes $j$ integral in the above strong sense, and fails to contain all of $O$.
--
--   Under this antecedent the conclusion is the following. For every field $F_{ss}$ that is an algebra over $\kappa_A$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` tracing $A$, with surjective residue map onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$ and satisfying the scaling normalisation), such that `R.integers` cuts out exactly $W_0$ on $F_0$, there exists a finite set $N_e$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa_A$ with the four properties:
--
--   (1) $N_e$ has exactly $q+1$ elements;
--
--   (2) a place $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ lies outside $N_e$ if and only if, for every $b\in B$ lying in `R.integers`, the $R$-residue of $b$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$;
--
--   (3) for every $Q\notin N_e$ there are a set $D$ of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and an element $z$ such that $R.\mathrm{IsResidueDisc}\,Q\,D\,z$ holds — $z$ is a disc coordinate (all places of $D$ are rational, $z$ has residue of absolute value $<1$ at them, $z$ lies in `R.integers` with $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ of its residue equal to $1$, every $c$ with $|c|<1$ is the value of $z$ at exactly one place of $D$, $z$ minus its value has order $1$ at each place of $D$, and the unit principle holds), and the pointwise and degree compatibilities hold, the latter equating the divisor degree over $D$ with $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ of the residue — such that moreover $j$ has no pole at any place of $D$ and every element of $B$ lies in the valuation subring of every place of $D$;
--
--   (4) for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is rational (the constants surject onto its residue field), if $P$ is centred at $s$, meaning that for every $f\in$ `R₀.integers` having poles only where $j$ has them and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s$ evaluated at that $R_0$-residue, the difference of $P$-value of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ — then either there is a node $O\in$ `nodes` contained in the valuation subring of $P$ and such that the $P$-value of every non-unit of $O$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$, or there are $Q\notin N_e$ and a residue disc $(D,z)$ for $Q$ in the above sense with $P\in D$.
--
--   This is the step, in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ over a valuation ring above $q$, which produces the $q+1$ ends of the base affine chart in the reduced field, the residue discs attached to the non-end places, and the dichotomy showing that every rational place centred at the supersingular place $s$ lies either over one of the $q+1$ nodes or in one of those discs. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep), which assembles the node presentations and node charts together with the Hasse germ of $j$ along the supersingular tube.
